WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Which skill should I use? Answer it once and keep the recommendation with the team.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
A public source becomes a team recommendation with its valid metadata and team context attached.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.500
Alex starts from a public repository or skill URL. Skills Board reads its valid SKILL.md.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:19.000
Alex adds the context only the team knows: a note, an example prompt, and tags.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.500
The public source, its metadata, and the team context are saved together.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.500
Alex saves it. Sam can find the same recommendation in the shared team library.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:32.500
Sam searches the library and finds Alex's recommendation with its context intact.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.000
Sam copies a prompt or compatible command while the original source stays visible.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Review the source, copy a compatible command, download the latest ZIP, or connect an authenticated agent through MCP.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:49.000
The next teammate finds the same answer, together with its source, notes, prompts, tags, and usage paths.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.000
One good recommendation stays with the team.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Save once. Find fast. Use it your way. Create your team library at skillsboard.sh.
